@startuml 12-sdd-boustrophedon-activity
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Diagram 12: Boustrophedon Coverage Path Algorithm
' SDD §7.1 — search_planner_node
' MC-SDD-001
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title "12 — Boustrophedon Coverage Path Algorithm\nsearch_planner_node  ·  SDD §7.1"

skinparam BackgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam DefaultFontColor #1C2334
skinparam DefaultFontSize 10
skinparam TitleFontSize 13
skinparam TitleFontStyle bold
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 5

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #D8E8F8
  BorderColor #3D5A80
  BorderThickness 1.5
  FontSize 10
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE8C0
  DiamondBorderColor #C07000
  DiamondFontSize 9
  ArrowColor #3D5A80
  ArrowFontSize 9
  ArrowFontColor #2A4060
  StartColor #1A3860
  EndColor #1A3860
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFAE8
  BorderColor #C09030
  FontSize 9
}

skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #8AA8C8
  TitleFontSize 10
  TitleFontStyle bold
}

|search_planner_node|

start

note right #FFE0E0
  <b>Status as of 2026-09-08: NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.</b>
  ws/src/mission_exec/src/search_planner_node.cpp is still a 15-line
  scaffold — its own header says so directly: "Scaffold only — the
  min-area bounding rectangle, sweep-line generation, and WGS-84
  back-projection land with the FCC-0xx implementation work." This
  diagram is the SDD §7.1 design to build against, not a description
  of current behaviour.
end note

:Receive  /mc/swarm/voronoi_cell
(cell polygon, ordered CCW vertices);

note right
  Triggered on:
  1. Initial VORONOI_PARTITION complete
  2. Re-partition due to peer loss
end note

:Load parameters from ROS 2 param server
  footprint_width_m  (default 20.0 m)
  overlap_fraction   (default 0.20)
  search_altitude_m  (default 50.0 m AGL)
  search_speed_ms    (default 5.0 m/s);

:Project cell polygon vertices
 from geodetic to local ENU Cartesian
 (origin = cell centroid, GeographicLib);

:Compute convex hull of cell polygon
 (gift-wrapping  O(n)  n = vertex count);

:Find minimum-area bounding rectangle
 of convex hull (rotating calipers  O(n))
 → sweep axis = longer rectangle edge;

:row_spacing = footprint_width_m × (1 − overlap_fraction)
 (default: 20.0 × 0.80 = 16.0 m);

:Generate parallel sweep lines
 perpendicular to sweep axis,
 spaced row_spacing apart,
 spanning full bounding rectangle extent;

repeat

  :Intersect next sweep line with cell polygon
   (Sutherland-Hodgman clip to polygon boundary);

  if (intersection non-empty?) then (yes)
    :Record row waypoint pair
     (entry_pt, exit_pt) in row_list[];
  else (no, sweep line outside cell)
  endif

repeat while (more sweep lines?) is (yes)

if (row_list empty?) then (yes)
  :Log error: cell too small for footprint width;
  :Publish empty coverage_path (manager retains HOLD);
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Order rows in boustrophedon pattern:
 row[0]: left → right
 row[1]: right → left  (swap entry/exit)
 row[2]: left → right  …;

note right
  Alternating direction minimises
  dead-transit between rows.
  Each row transition adds one
  altitude-offset waypoint (+5 m AGL)
  to clear obstacles during turn.
end note

:Insert transition waypoints between rows:
 after each row exit_pt → climb +5 m AGL
 waypoint (type: LOITER_TURNS n=0)
 before descending to next row entry_pt;

:Back-project all Cartesian waypoints
 to geodetic (lat, lon, alt_msl)
 (alt_msl = terrain_alt + search_altitude_m);

:Annotate each waypoint:
  acceptance_radius = row_spacing / 2
  waypoint_speed    = search_speed_ms
  frame             = MAV_FRAME_GLOBAL_RELATIVE_ALT;

:Choose path start waypoint:
 nearest waypoint to drone's current position
 (Euclidean distance in ENU frame)
 → minimise dead transit from muster point;

:Publish  /mc/search/coverage_path
 (mc_msgs/CoveragePathStamped)
 N waypoints, ordered from start;

note right
  Typical values for 500 m × 500 m cell:
  row_spacing = 16 m  → ~31 rows
  Waypoints per path ≈ 62 transit + 31 transitions = ~93 total
  Computation time ≤ 5 s  [PR-008]
end note

|mission_manager_node|

:Receive  /mc/search/coverage_path;

:Format as PX4 mission items
 (MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT per point
  MAV_CMD_NAV_LOITER_TURNS for transitions);

:Upload mission to FCC via fcc_bridge_node
 (MAVLink mission upload protocol);

:Command FCC: SET_MODE AUTO → MISSION;

|search_planner_node|

stop

@enduml
